<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gurdit Singh (Ladwa)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1763</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gurdit Singh was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> sardar who seized Ladwa and nearby lands near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurukshetra">Kurukshetra</a> around 1763, when the Sikh misls overran the Mughal province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirhind">Sirhind</a>. His chiefship became one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cis-sutlej-states">Cis-Sutlej states</a> under British protection from 1809. His descendant Ajit Singh sided with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a> army in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-sikh-war">First Anglo-Sikh War</a>, and Ladwa was confiscated in 1846.</p></div>
